    "body": "Priority: P2/P3 pending reproduction. `tooling/scripts/gen-docs.mjs`, `tooling/scripts/check-migrations.mjs` and `tooling/perf/summary.mjs` compare a resolved argv entry spelling with a loader-realpathed module URL. A self-contained Node 22.23.4 junction probe confirms these spellings can differ, making this lexical guard false. Actual pnpm invocation and repository gate bypass have NOT been reproduced. CI used real directories; no current CI result is invalidated by this observation.\n\nPotential impact: invoking the scripts through an alias may exit zero before doing their work, including docs or migration checks.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Reproduce actual supported pnpm commands from a disposable aliased checkout, with deliberate invalid generated docs/migration inputs as discriminating negative controls.\n- Record direct versus alias argv/cwd behavior and exit/output; distinguish a direct Node invocation from an actual pnpm gate path.\n- If the defect is reachable, fix entry dispatch and add bounded regressions for each affected command; otherwise record why the actual invocation is safe and close with evidence.\n- Preserve inert import and normal direct invocation; do not change gate thresholds or owner files.\n\nDeferred because these are pre-existing tooling entry points outside #435's launcher helper contract. Review observation O1.\n\nOrigin: Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh formal scan 1 of PR #492 at `6f383da798872aa0e6bd1e0de1fdcd4e702de9ae` (full report in the PR conversation). Open and closed issue searches for symlink, entry, inert and artifact found no matching root cause.\n\nDisposition: DEFER-ISSUE; parked under `backlog`, with no pickup gate. This follow-up does not expand the authorized four-intent batch or block #435. Preserve docs/15 delivery and independent opposite-family review when separately dispatched.\n",
